{
    block: "forgeweave:faucet",
    decoder: "block_entity",
    expect: {
        drained: {
            amount: 25,
            id: "forgeweave:molten_iron"
        },
        id: "forgeweave:faucet",
        redstone: 0b,
        stop: 0b
    },
    nbt: {
        drained: {
            amount: 25,
            id: "forgeweave:molten_iron"
        },
        id: "forgeweave:faucet",
        stop: 0b
    },
    what: "M2 (#100): a faucet caught mid-pour, in the shape M2 wrote it -- a buffered drain of molten iron and no `redstone` key at all, because redstone activation (#207) had not been added yet. This is the one M3 block-entity format whose tag actually changed shape, and it changed twice: #200 made `drained` unconditional so an idle faucet's update packet stops being empty, and #207 added `redstone`. Both are read back through defaults (`getCompound` of a missing key is empty, `getBoolean` of a missing key is false), and the `expect` above is what M3 writes for this same faucet -- the migration, pinned."
}
